{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit built-in uniform priors for the finite-bounded parameters `mean_lambda`, `sigma_proc`, `sigma_obs`, and `N_est1`, matching the implicit bounded uniform priors indicated by the original parameter constraints/comments. This satisfies SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one prior sampling statement before use. The parameter `lambda` already had its built-in normal prior. No data copies or reshapes were needed; `data_safe.json` is unchanged from the supplied data. `T` remains an unprotected context input.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> T;
  vector[T] y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=10> mean_lambda; // Mean growth rate
  real<lower=0, upper=10> sigma_proc; // SD of state process
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_obs; // SD of observation process
  vector<lower=0>[T - 1] lambda;
  real<lower=0, upper=500> N_est1; // Initial population size
}
transformed parameters {
  vector<lower=0>[T] N_est;

  N_est[1] = N_est1;
  // State process
  for (t in 1 : (T - 1)) {
    N_est[t + 1] = N_est[t] * lambda[t];
  }
}
model {
  // Explicit priors matching the original bounded implicit priors
  mean_lambda ~ uniform(0, 10);
  sigma_proc ~ uniform(0, 10);
  sigma_obs ~ uniform(0, 100);
  N_est1 ~ uniform(0, 500);

  // State process
  lambda ~ normal(mean_lambda, sigma_proc);

  // Observation process
  y ~ normal(N_est, sigma_obs);
}
generated quantities {
  real<lower=0> sigma2_obs;
  real<lower=0> sigma2_proc;

  sigma2_obs = square(sigma_obs);
  sigma2_proc = square(sigma_proc);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"T":1,"y":[5.781370246206928]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
